# This file is for production deployment only
# Do NOT commit real secrets
#
# HOW TO FILL THIS FILE:
# ----------------------
# 1) Prefer setting these in Vercel (or your host) → Project → Settings → Environment Variables → Production.
# 2) NEXT_PUBLIC_* are embedded in the browser bundle — never put database passwords or server master keys there.
# 3) NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_API_KEY must match backend ADMIN_API_KEY (same random value you set on the API host).
#    Copy the backend value from your secret manager / Railway variables — do not invent a second key.
# 4) next build with NODE_ENV=production can load .env.production; for local prod smoke tests use .env.production.local
#    (gitignored) instead of committing filled values.
#
# Step-by-step:
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL: your public FastAPI base URL (same origin you configured in backend CORS ALLOWED_ORIGINS).
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: Google Cloud Console → OAuth Web client → Client ID (same as backend GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID).
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_API_KEY: paste exact same string as backend ADMIN_API_KEY.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Final checklist (before go-live)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [ ] Database connected (backend health / app loads data)
# [ ] Google login works (OAuth consent + authorized JavaScript origins = your Vercel URL)
# [ ] RFQ email works (backend RESEND_* configured; test submit from site)
# [ ] Admin access secured (admin key only in env; rotate if ever exposed)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# What: Browser-visible base URL for all client-side API calls to FastAPI.
# Where: Your deployed backend URL (Railway public domain or custom API domain).
# Format: https://api.yourdomain.com — no trailing slash.
# Set here so a blank line never overrides Vercel; override per-environment in Vercel if needed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.advancedsystems-int.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_API_KEY=advanced-secret-123
# What: Google Sign-In client ID for the One Tap / GIS script in the browser.
# Where: Same credential as backend GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (Google Cloud Console → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID).
# Format: xxxxx-xxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# Do not set empty NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID= here — it would override Vercel. Set only in Vercel (Production).

# What: Must equal backend ADMIN_API_KEY (shared secret for admin `api-key` header from the browser).
# Where: Copy from Railway/backend env after you set ADMIN_API_KEY there — do not generate a different value.
# Format: long random string (same as backend).
# Do not set empty NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_API_KEY= here — it would override Vercel. Set only in Vercel (Production).

# Server-only: Next.js API routes (e.g. enrich-products proxy) — set in Vercel without NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# Should match backend ADMIN_API_KEY if those routes forward that header.
# ADMIN_API_KEY=
